    "['local-user [parameter1] service-type [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'snmp-server user nms2-admin group grp1 v3 auth sha priv aes', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'snmp-server user nms2-admin group grp1 v3 auth sha priv aes', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nsnmp-server user nms2-admin group grp1 v3 auth sha priv aes\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Huawei `local-user nms2-admin service-type snmp` command creates an SNMP user and assigns service permissions.\\n- The Cisco equivalent creates an SNMPv3 user (`nms2-admin` in this case), assigns it to a group (`grp1`), specifies v3 security level, and sets authentication (SHA) and privacy (AES) protocols.\\n- Note that the actual passwords/keys would need to be configured separately in Cisco, typically using the `snmp-server group` and `snmp-server view` commands for full equivalence.', 'trans_template': None}]]": 1,
