    "['task-group [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'privilege exec level 10 snmp-server', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'privilege exec level 10 snmp-server', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"For the given HUAWEI command `task-group tg1`, the equivalent Cisco command would involve creating a privilege level or role-based access control (RBAC) configuration. However, Cisco does not have a direct 1:1 equivalent for HUAWEI's `task-group`. The closest approximation would be to define a **privilege level** or **custom view** (for SNMP access control).\\n\\nThe translation would be:\\n##\\nprivilege exec level 10 snmp-server\\n##\\n(Note: Cisco's implementation is less granular than HUAWEI's task-group approach. The exact privilege level (e.g., 10) would depend on your Cisco device's existing RBAC structure. For modern IOS-XE, you might use `role-based` CLI views instead.)\", 'trans_template': None}]]": 1,
